   "he": "אֲבָל הַזּוֹב. זוֹב מְנָלַן? דְּתַנְיָא: ״זוֹבוֹ טָמֵא״ — לִימֵּד עַל הַזּוֹב שֶׁהוּא טָמֵא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «But ziva» transmits impurity when moist, although not when dry. The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive that «ziva» transmits impurity? «As it is taught» in a baraita that discusses the verse: “When any man has an issue out of his flesh, «his issue,» it is «impure”» (Leviticus 15:2). This «taught with regard to ziva that it is impure.»"
